### Edit 1 — Evaluation TXT: status marker for non-success messages
In `formatEvaluationAsText`, in the message loop, after `Time` line, add:
```js
const status = String(message?.status || "").trim().toLowerCase();
if (status && status !== "success") {
  const reason = String(message?.failureReason || "").trim();
  lines.push(`Status   : ${status}${reason ? ` (${reason})` : ""}`);
}
```
This renders `Status   : failed (The generation failed)` or `Status   : stopped`. Empty failed messages still show `(empty)` content — now with the Status line explaining why.

### Edit 2 — Evaluation JSON: warn about non-success assistant messages
In `buildJsonExportObject` (evaluation branch), before returning:
```js
const warnings = [t("attachment_warning")];
const nonSuccess = (Array.isArray(record?.messages) ? record.messages : []).filter(
  (m) => String(m?.role || "").toLowerCase() === "assistant" &&
