### Edit 3 — Agent TXT: per-message time fallback to metadata.timing.completedAt
In `formatAgentAsText`:
```js
const messageTime = message?.createdAt || message?.metadata?.timing?.completedAt;
if (messageTime) {
  lines.push(`Time     : ${formatTextTime(messageTime)}`);
}
```
`formatTextTime` does `new Date(value)` — for epoch ms number 1790156651083, `String(1790156651083)` → `new Date("1790156651083")` → Invalid Date! Because formatTextTime stringifies first. So I need to convert: `new Date(Number(ms)).toISOString()` when it's a number. Let me write a helper:
```js
function formatMessageTime(message) {
  const createdAt = message?.createdAt;
  if (createdAt) return formatTextTime(createdAt);
  const completedAt = message?.metadata?.timing?.completedAt;
  if (completedAt) {
    const date = new Date(Number(completedAt));
    if (!Number.isNaN(date.getTime())) return formatTextTime(date.toISOString());
  }
  return "";
}
```
